## LCS🔗

A common subsequence of two strings is a subsequence that is common to both strings. For e.g. `ace` is a subsequence of `abcde`

We are supposed to find the Longest Common Subsequence between two strings.

This is clearly a 2D DP problem, as both `(i, j)` define the state of problem at any moment in time.

Recurrence Relation

\[ \begin{align} P(i, j) &= 1 + P(i+1, j+1), \text{ when } s[i] == s[j] \\ P(i, j) &= max(P(i, j+1), P(i+1, j)) \end{align} \]

Solution : 

```
def main(s1, s2):
    n, m = len(s1), len(s2)

    @cache
    def lcs(i, j):

        if i >= n or j >= m:
            return 0

        if s1[i] == s2[j]:
            return 1 + lcs(i+1, j+1)

        return max(lcs(i, j+1), lcs(i+1, j))

    return lcs(0, 0)

```

